Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:58:36 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 091/110] Arc import: a space's tabs in its Arc profile's
 profile

Onboarding imports the sidebar before the sign-ins, so the open tabs of a
space in another Arc profile were made before that profile existed, in the
main one. Every tab opened from the sidebar then took the active tab as its
source and followed it there, so the whole space was signed in as the main
profile, also after a restart.

- The import loads its spaces' profiles before making their tabs.
- What the browser opens (the sidebar, a menu) takes the active space's
  profile, not the active tab's; a page's links keep their page's.
- Tabs outside their space's profile move into it at startup, unloaded and
  not archived (repairs 0.5.13's imports).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
